  "rulings": {
    "references": [
      {
        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=EX8-073#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for EX8-073 (Jan. 10, 2025)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "The effects trigger simultaneously, so the player can choose the activation order.",
        "question": "Multiple effects trigger when this card digivolves. In what order do they activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  If your opponent has a Digimon with 10000 DP or less, you must choose that card and delete it.",
        "question": "My opponent has a Digimon with 10000 DP or less.  Can I meet the \"if this effect didn't delete\" condition in this card's [When Digivolving] [End of Attack] effect by not choosing a card to delete?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, you can.",
        "question": "My opponent has a Digimon with 10000 DP or less.  Can I meet the \"if this effect didn't delete\" condition in this card's [When Digivolving] [End of Attack] effect by choosing an opponent's Digimon with 10000 DP or less and an effect that prevents deletion?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "It refers to when the memory gauge is at 0 or further to the right.",
        "question": "What position on the memory gauge does \"while you have 0 or less\" memory refer to?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "This effect prevents Digimon from being affected by effects.  For example, your Digmon won't suspend if it's chosen for a \"suspend 1 of your opponent's Digimon\" effect, and its DP won't be reduced if it's chosen for a \"1 of your opponent's Digimon gets -3000 DP\" effect.",
        "question": "What does \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" mean, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it can be chosen.",
        "question": "Can a card that has an \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect be chosen for an effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it can.  However, it won't be affected by it.",
        "question": "Can a card that has an \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect be given an effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "As soon as it gains the \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect, it will no longer be affected.",
        "question": "If a card is affected by an effect, then it later gains an \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect, what happens to the effect that was affecting it?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "It will be affected by the effect as soon as it can be affected by effects.",
        "question": "If a card has an \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect, it gains an effect, then it later loses the \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect, what happens to the effect that it gained?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, it doesn’t trigger.  If an effect is given to a Digimon that isn't affected by effects, it won't trigger.",
        "question": "A card that has an \"isn't affected by [...] effects\" effect was given an effect that triggers at a timing such as [When Attacking].  Will the effect trigger if that card later meets the trigger conditions?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
